# The foundational vocabulary shared across the mathematics library. The base of everything is the set (a collection of
# distinct things) and the function (a map between sets). On top sit the algebraic structures (magma, semigroup, monoid,
# group, ring, field), the spaces (topological, metric, vector, inner-product, Hilbert, manifold), and the categorical
# view (objects and morphisms). Every later file builds on these. This file is the index of that foundation; the
# definitions live in the structure, space, and theory folders, and the machine-checked theorems live in the number,
# polynomial, order, and algebra-tower files.
